BT /F1 13 Tf 50 682 Td (Test types) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 659 Td (Baseline: one user at a time to establish normal response times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 643 Td (Load: increase gradually to the expected demo or initial user traffic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 627 Td (Stress: increase beyond expected load to identify the failure point and recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 611 Td (Soak: maintain modest traffic to detect leaks or slow degradation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 50 575 Td (Safe test procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 552 Td (1. Use a local/staging environment and synthetic test accounts only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 536 Td (2. Record app version, machine, database size, AI model, and test settings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 520 Td (3. Warm up, run each scenario at set concurrency, then repeat for consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 504 Td (4. Separate AI provider wait from app, template, and database processing time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 488 Td (5. Stop if errors rise sharply or provider limits are approached.) Tj ET
